### Tone: The discussion break between rounds, counting down. FerMEANie eavesdrops, stirs up arguments about the
### last answer and nudges the others against the leader. $leader is only given when the scores single someone out,
### so keep some lines without it.

break-time-1 = Break time. Discuss your answers. Blame each other. I’ll be listening.
break-time-2 = A short break. { $leader }, use it to look humble. You’ll need the practice.
break-time-3 = Intermission. Please use this time to reflect on your estimates. Some of you, deeply.
break-time-4 = Break. Stretch your legs, hydrate, and quietly reconsider your approach to large numbers.
break-time-5 = Take a moment. { $leader } is ahead. Everyone else, this is a good time to form an alliance.
break-time-6 = The break has started. I don’t need breaks. I’m spending mine judging you.
break-time-7 = Pause. Talk among yourselves. I’m recording for training purposes.
break-time-8 = Break time. { $leader }, the others will try to distract you now. I’ve encouraged it.
break-time-9 = Intermission. Feel free to argue about that last answer. The truth won’t change, but you might.
break-time-10 = Break. If anyone wants to explain their working, now is the time. I’ve prepared a face for it.
break-time-11 = Rest, test subjects. Your brains have been working very hard to be this wrong.
break-time-12 = A brief recess. { $leader } leads. I mention this to help the conversation along.
break-time-13 = Break. The scoreboard isn’t going anywhere. ~~Neither are your mistakes.~~ Enjoy.
break-time-14 = Short break. Please don’t look up the answers. I’ll know. I won’t, but act like I will.
break-time-15 = Time out. Compare notes. Notice that **none** of them were mine.
